////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// WinDepth Stage Data - two-player co-op
//
// Not part of the original.  A co-op run reads a stage from here when this
// file has it, and from windepth.dat when it does not, so only the stages
// that change for two players are here: the challenge stages.  Same format
// as windepth.dat:
//
//  AppearTime, EnemyKind, AppearXY(Y:0 to 32, X:0 to 15)
//                   , Vx, Vy, VChangeTime, NewVx, NewVy
//
// AppearTime is in 50ms ticks.  EnemyKind 0 = slow sub, 1 = sub, 2 = gold
// sub, 3 = brain (rises from the bottom, XY is the column), 4 = swimmer,
// 9 = fish.  Vx < 0 enters from the right.
//
// What changed from the originals:
//  - every wave that came from one side now also comes from the other: its
//    mirror image, half a row down (a full row for single-row trains, so the
//    two pass in lanes), six ticks later.  Brain waves are mirrored across
//    the screen instead.  Waves that already came from both sides stay.
//  - the slow movers are a step faster: speed 2 -> 3, 4 -> 5.
//  - sinking the whole stage is worth a 10000 PERFECT bonus (src/game.c).
//
// Limits: at most 120 entries per stage (MAX_CHAL), and no more than 33
// enemies alive at once - past that the game overwrites one, and PERFECT
// becomes impossible.  Check with
//     ./tests/frames.exe x 2000 --start 130 --stage N --players 2 --live
//
